<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Briggs Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Briggs Plan was the British strategy against the communist insurgency in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> devised in 1950 by Lieutenant-General Sir Harold Briggs, the director of operations during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malayan-emergency">Malayan Emergency</a>. It resettled about half a million rural Chinese squatters into guarded new villages to cut the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a> off from food, recruits and information, and coordinated police, army and civil administration. Continued under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-templer">Gerald Templer</a>, it contributed to the insurgents' defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/briggs-plan.jpg" alt="Briggs Plan" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Village_in_Malaya,_1950s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
